组件系统 README · then restart dsh web and hard-refresh the browser (Ctrl+Shift+R)：- **The session, live** — turns · steps, context level and compaction, tokens and cache hit rate, LLM time, first-token latency, tool calls, background jobs and subagents;
- **Money and quota** — OpenCode Go's rolling / weekly / monthly windows; Command Code's 5-hour / weekly / monthly limits with one tap to cycle the whole key pool, its credit balances, a month-end projection and today's budget;
- **Time, and the official wallet** — a Clock (analog or digital, six zones), a Calendar that dots the days DSH has a scheduled task on (2×2 month grid; 2×4 adds the upcoming list), a Task Timer for the running turn and what it is waiting on, a Stopwatch you can start / pause / reset, a Countdown (duration capsules or the next scheduled task), and the DeepSeek balance card with the ledger-derived day's spend beside it;
- **The machine** — CPU / GPU / memory / disk / network / power, with sparklines, rings and a local-service plus proxy-egress board;
- **Your own view** — every card is an independent unit: install it, size it 2×2 or 2×4, tune its thresholds, or switch it off. The rail packs the rest.

组件系统 README · Component Marketplace：- Browse all widgets (system + external), search, size-switch preview, install per `widget@size`;
- The installed list supports drag-reorder, config editing, and one-click `2×2 ↔ 2×4` (auto-dedup — one instance per widget/size);
- The widget-config tab supports per-card customization (quote of the day, heatmap window alignment, etc.).

组件系统 README · Pooled accounts — tap a card to switch：- **Tap any Command Code card to cycle** `AllUser → Physicolor → Sparxie → AllUser`. The view is persisted per card instance (`cardConfigs.ccView`), so the choice survives a reload — and it is deliberately a different field from the OpenCode pool's `poolView`, so the two families never share a view;
- **`AllUser` is the pool's total**, summed field by field: a window's percent is `sum(used) / sum(cap)` (a mean of percents would call one exhausted pool beside an untouched pool "50% used"), the monthly window sums each member's own month — each measured against **its own** plan, so a two-GOAT pool is 2 × $70 — and the account card shows the generic `AllUser` label with the member names beneath it. `AllUser` is deliberately the same literal in both languages;
- **The legend line carries the current view** (`Account · AllUser`, `Windows · Physicolor`) beside the card's role word, and the hover tooltip spells out the whole chain;
- **One key configured → no switcher at all**: the cards render exactly as they did before, with the bare role word and the account name in the body. Two pools resolving to the same account name are disambigu

组件系统 README · Compatibility：- DeepSeek Harness `0.1.0-rc.6` and later `0.1.x`, plus `0.2.0-rc.1` and later `0.2.x` — in the browser and in the desktop app;
- Integrates via `conversation.input.overlay` / `conversation.session.header.utilities` / `conversation.composer.dock` / `settings.section`;
- Coordinates explicitly with `dsh-better-sidebar`'s right rail: the rail reads the official right-bar column (keeping `--dsh-sidebar-width` as a fallback for older better-sidebar builds) and its header capsule registers at `order: 5` so the two toggles cannot swap places on a bundle reload; no residue after uninstall.

组件系统 README · What's new — v1.8.5：- **The time family** — a **Clock** (analog or digital, six zones, a second hand that ticks), a **Calendar** that dots the days DSH has a scheduled task on (2×2 month grid; the 2×4 adds the upcoming list), a **Task Timer** for the running turn and what it is waiting on, a **Stopwatch** you can start / pause / reset, and a **Countdown** (duration capsules, or the next scheduled task);
- **DeepSeek balance** — the official account balance with the ledger-derived day's spend beside it, reading a host route of its own (`/api/deepseek-balance`), with the fold covered by a new offline gate;
- **A declared data-source contract** — a unit says what it reads (`reads`, `source`, its skeleton) and one generic poller answers for all of them; the build now fails when a declaration drifts from the unit;
- **Four defects gone** — the hover wave no longer arms a whole row below the pointer on a rail another plugin has pushed down (45 checks: 25 FAIL → 45/45 PASS); the session-header anchor stops freezing when the shell swaps its node; the whole-card rule and the wheel's end detent read the same measured inset — and `paneH` is measured at all, which it never had be

组件系统 README · Roadmap：- **Heatmap token accounting follow-up**: the card's total already equals dsh-usage-center's (the host route reuses its `getActivity()`). Making it exact when usage-center is *not* installed would mean folding the same session logs inside this host — deliberately not duplicated today, to keep one caliber maintained in one place;
- **Command Code monthly window, pending an upstream field**: the month is derived locally as `used = plan allowance − remaining monthly credits` (allowance from the published plan table) because `billing/credits` returns no monthly window object. If upstream later adds `monthly` (with used / cap / resetAt) to `windowLimits`, `monthlyWindow()` should read it directly and keep the derivation only as a fallback;
- **Command Code pool discovery by naming convention**: the host reads `COMMANDCODE_API_KEY` plus the `_2 … _4` spares that the provider's Account-rotation card writes. A key stored under an unrelated ref name would need that ref added to `COMMANDCODE_POOL_ENVS` (the credentials service exposes `resolve(ref)` only — there is no "list the refs" seam to enumerate them);
